**Required output format (plan-state contract — MANDATORY):**

End the response with EXACTLY ONE of these labels on its own line and emit
nothing after it:

state:plan-go
state:plan-no-go
state:plan-blocked

Write the label as plain text. Do not put the label in a code fence, a block
quote, or any other container. A code fence leaves its closing marker as the
final line, and the parser then rejects the whole review. Do not repeat the
label earlier in the response, because the parser accepts exactly one.

Use `state:plan-blocked` only when planning cannot proceed without human
feedback or an external dependency. The prose before the final label must say
why it is blocked, identify any blocking issue, and state what unblocks it.